  "id": "COMPOUND:11914 - PROTEIN:1442",
  "verbalization": "Butylparaben appears to have a shared target of DNA polymerase alpha subunit B through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Butylparaben may interact with Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic, which is targeted by 3-Epicaryoptin and Chinikomycin B, both of which are linked to DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. This implies a potential chain of interactions where Butylparaben could influence the activity of Serine--tRNA ligase, which in turn affects DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The presence of multiple targets and their shared relationship with DNA polymerase alpha subunit B suggests a possible mechanism involving the modulation of RNA synthesis or protein function through these intermediaries. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of these intermediaries in mediating the effect of Butylparaben on DNA polymerase alpha subunit B.",
